    {
      "id": "hg-porosimetry-gdl::n10",
      "iri": "https://w3id.org/h2kg/decode/workflow/hg-porosimetry-gdl/node/n10",
      "source_id": "n10",
      "label": "MPL parameter estimation from GDL and substrate data",
      "native_category": "",
      "description": "MPL parameter estimation from GDL and substrate data\nOwner: Bosch:Matthias Hanauer\nTask: T2.1\nMaturity: established method\nDocumentation: following simple formulas are used:MPL thickness estimation: L_MPL = L_GDL - L_sub.MPL conductivity estimation: sigma_MPL = L_MPL / ( L_GDL/sigma_TP,GDL - L_sub/sigma_TP,sub).MPL permeability estimation: kappa_MPL = L_MPL / ( L_GDL/kappa_TP,GDL - L_sub/kappa_TP,sub).Correction of in-plane permeability in substrate (due to partial MPL intrusion): kappa_IP,sub = (kappa_IP,GDL*L_GDL - kappa_MPL*L_MPL)/L_sub.MPL porosity estimation: eps_MPL = (L_GDL*eps_GDL - L_sub*eps_sub)/L_MPL.Estimation of average pore radius': Through visual inspection of GDL and substrate pore size distributions, identifying the MPL contribution as main difference between the two, and possibly using the large-pore region from the GDL data for refining the substrate pore radius.\nRange of validity or processability: \nAccuracy/validity depends strongly on the specific material, and especially on the extent to which MPL material intrudes into the substrate. Results should be validated against other methods (i.e. property estimations based on tomography data)\ninternal key: MPL parameter estimation from GDL and substrate data0",
      "shape": "hexagon",
      "kind": "occurrence",
      "workflow_id": "hg-porosimetry-gdl",
      "visual_category": "method",
      "mapping_state": "reviewed_decode",
      "anchor_id": "https://w3id.org/h2kg/decode/workflow/anchor/mpl-parameter-estimation-from-gdl-and-substrate-data-method",
      "decision": "reviewed_decode_anchor",
      "canonical_role_iri": "https://w3id.org/h2kg/hydrogen-ontology#Measurement",
      "semantic_role": "Measurement",
      "confidence": "reviewed_structural",
      "mapping_evidence": "DECODE-specific concept retained as a stable reviewed anchor. Its source topology is preserved; no H2KG synonym or new public term was asserted."
